    "    nodes\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aa885492-cbd7-45a5-97d2-28136e6bc7df",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Remark.** Node names are shown directly where space allows, while numbered labels are used in denser portions of the network to avoid overlapping text. Thicker corridors indicate larger passenger flow values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e5a036e2-4b1d-419a-a424-228f2b3aa8c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Maximum-Flow with Rail Expansion\n",
    "\n",
    "The baseline maximum-flow solution routes 2,900 passengers per hour into `Downtown`. If downtown-bound demand is expected to exceed this level, one possible response is to add higher-capacity transit infrastructure.\n",
    "\n",
    "To test this idea, two rapid-transit rail lines are added to the network. The Canada Line connects `MarineCambie` to `Downtown` through the Cambie corridor, while the Expo/Millennium Line connects `KingswayBoundary` to `Downtown` through the Kingsway and Main corridors.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because these rail lines have substantially higher passenger capacity than the existing bus routes, they create new high-capacity connections into `Downtown`. The expanded network is then reoptimized with the same source nodes and destinations to measure the effect on maximum passenger flow."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0deb7a76-d978-438a-8d06-186c3fc50f4e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "OPTIMAL LP SOLUTION FOUND\n",
      "Wrote solution to outputs/sol_maxflow_expansion.txt\n",
      "Model has been successfully processed\n",
      "SOURCE flow:\n",
      "     MarineGranville           -1400\n",
      "           MarineOak            -300\n",
      "        MarineCambie           -2600\n",
      "        KnightMarine            -600\n",
      "      MarineBoundary              -0\n",
      "    KingswayBoundary           -5700\n",
      "    LougheedBoundary            -600\n",
      "         Boundary1st              -0\n",
      "    BoundaryHastings            -600\n",
      "SINK flow:\n",
      "            Downtown           10100\n",
      "                 UBC            1700\n",
      "Total flow: 11800 passengers/hour\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "result = run_glpk(\n",
    "    \"models/maxflow.mod\",\n",
    "    \"data/maxflow_expansion.dat\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print_glpk_block(\n",
    "    result,\n",
    "    start_label=\"SOURCE flow:\",\n",
    "    end_label=\"Total flow:\"\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "25ec6f4b-4591-4de8-a92f-c9023feea3be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The added rail lines increase maximum total flow from **4,600 to 11,800 passengers per hour**. This increase occurs entirely in the flow directed toward `Downtown`, which rises from **2,900 to 10,100 passengers per hour**, while flow into `UBC` remains unchanged.\n",
    "\n",
    "The plot below shows how the optimized flow is routed through the expanded network."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "289b2410-46bb-404b-bd84-3941746cc477",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1150x750 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "plot_flow_network(\n",
    "    \"outputs/sol_maxflow_expansion.txt\",\n",
    "    \"Maximum-Flow Routing with Rail Expansion\",\n",
    "    nodes\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2611b24f-7acb-4606-91ed-8206491469d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The added rail lines allow for substantially larger passenger flow into `Downtown`. This comparison shows how optimization can help planners estimate the capacity impact of a proposed infrastructure change."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8db368f9-cca3-40a3-bbf9-29736e86e9ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Minimum-Cost Routing to UBC\n",
    "\n",
    "The previous models focused on maximizing passenger flow through the network. In practice, transit planners may also need to find cost-efficient ways to satisfy an estimated level of passenger demand. \n",
    "\n",
    "For this scenario, 2,500 passengers per hour must be routed into `UBC`. This demand is supplied by five source nodes — `MarineGranville`, `MarineOak`, `MarineCambie`, `KingswayBoundary`, and `BoundaryHastings` — each contributing 500 passengers per hour.\n",
    "\n",
    "The analysis is performed on the expanded transit network with the added rail infrastructure.\n",
    "\n",
    "Transportation cost is modeled at a rate of \\$0.10 per kilometer traveled for each passenger moving through the system. As a result, corridors carrying larger numbers of passengers over longer distances incur higher total cost.\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective is to find the minimum-cost routing that satisfies the required UBC-bound demand."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5665cc66-dcb6-4f64-9ac0-3b7f5dfaf8b3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "OPTIMAL LP SOLUTION FOUND\n",
      "Wrote solution to outputs/sol_mincost_ubc.txt\n",
      "Total cost: 3767 $\n",
      "Model has been successfully processed\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "result = run_glpk(\n",
    "    \"models/mincost_ubc.mod\",\n",
    "    \"data/mincost_ubc.dat\"\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "14eb32e8-51b2-4020-adec-ddb223217558",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The minimum-cost solution satisfies the required UBC-bound demand with a total transportation cost of approximately **\\$3,767 per hour**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The plot below shows the lowest-cost routing pattern through the network. Flow values for individual corridors are saved in `outputs/sol_mincost_ubc.txt`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5bcb871b-50a2-4133-b1a8-ec13135f870e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
