    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "plot_multicommodity_flow(\n",
    "    \"outputs/sol_mincost_multi_destination.txt\",\n",
    "    \"Multi-Destination Minimum-Cost Routing\",\n",
    "    nodes\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "43d5261f-6177-488f-971c-a6ffdf4027a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
     "In a minimum-cost routing model, dual values can be used to estimate where additional capacity would most reduce total cost. Here, they provide a sensitivity measure for the corridor-capacity constraints." 
     "\n",
     "These values estimate how total routing cost would change if a corridor’s capacity were increased slightly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7f9bf6a4-8510-4bf6-8e75-acaf784a86c8",
   "metadata": {},
